5 (c) Any municipal solid waste facility operator may
6 apply for the funds associated with the carcass management
7 project listed as priority 1 in subsection (b) of this
8 section. Funds for the carcass management project shall be
9 expended only for infrastructure necessary to haul, bury or
10 compost dead animals. Funds expended under this subsection
11 shall not exceed the amount listed in priority 1 in
12 subsection (b) of this section.
13
14 (d) The department of environmental quality may
15 modify the authorized funds and the order of the projects
16 listed in the prioritized list contained in subsection (b)
17 of this section for any of the following reasons:
18
19 (i) To optimize efficiency;
20
21 (ii) Based on project readiness;
22
4 HB0014

2025 STATE OF WYOMING 25LSO-0198
1 (iii) Based on compliance with grant or loan
2 qualifications or conditions;
3
4 (iv) To address emergency or immediate
5 environmental concerns.
6
7 (e) Not later than October 15 of each year, the
8 department of environmental quality shall report:
9
10 (i) Any modification of the prioritized list
11 contained in subsection (b) of this section to the joint
12 minerals, business and economic development interim
13 committee and the joint appropriations committee;
14
15 (ii) The names of recipients and amounts
16 expended for the carcass management project established by
17 priority 1 in subsections (b) and (c) of this section to
18 the joint minerals, business and economic development
19 interim committee.
20
21 Section 2. 2024 Wyoming Session Laws, Chapter 32 is
22 repealed.
